COAX_RELAY_DETAILS :: "65b7|65b710d3add3022d9f4b77e793da9ea1432710c33a0119b4d212cba956fee94b||The main Coax roadmap: what gets built in what order so OpenAgents and Metareal can express computation, data, protocols, tools and build policy in Coax, with costs and ownership visible. Milestones have dependencies and exit evidence, not dates.\\n\\nSpecification: coax/ROADMAP.md in the openagents repository.||\n6f40|6f40bdaaf4012eddd207f37bd5269b7300cb47d982738a2981433b500ffc8f35||Real engine kernels and the whole development loop measured against frozen references, original-source debugging, one release/status source and an independently enforced review gate. Exit: reproducible kernel and whole-loop reports, no unexpected output or allocation regressions, usable native debugging, a versioned baseline.||\nd98b|d98bd18d14eb90c38974a688a4d41d3917764e2a8a69fd5082dca321a24681cb||R1a first: declaration and content identities, explicit targets, original spans, basic namespaces and inspectable procedure lowering, pinned by differential fixtures. R1b scheduling and configuration follow.||\n08f5|08f57f4e5b411eee3cea11793e980103f99b6afb6d2afc45211d9b93046e855c||R2a first: tagged results and optionals, exhaustive switching, propagation and cleanup; a shared asynchronous host contract with R3.||\n27ad|27ad3acadab3d706b6accf79869f8d2eea208d65e92768a7782aaa8eadba8b4a||R3a started (E0383 rejects simple returns of borrows into local arrays). Then typed transfer, deferred destruction and owning storage (R3b).||\na0eb|a0eb08dcf5fe3170ed7f027b1aeadbc74dfaf86fb94eaa32634f5bbd014e7065||R4a first: generic copyable values and non-owning operations over fixed storage; owning libraries wait for R3b.||\n265f|265f90e30e9a84da1061c584a4b233dc5117f000fcd289bcbf518d9d28a35075||R5a first: narrow derivation over concrete, already-checked types.||\n1ca0|1ca0f77a097e3a712ed32ce996a2d73c0535b0da6a6923ad1a7b2311eeb29a34||Phase-typed Code, quotation, #insert and #expand with hygiene and expansion budgets.||\na989|a9896a04fd5c4adb8f4e3697e37f59328f0ce7c5db0b5944f68185f4fa6623d2||R7a: formatting, evidence, typed queries and revision-bound fixes early, on current APIs. R7b: workspaces, typed plugins and build programming.||\nc1fb|c1fbb24e4aa29cd70974f45bfafbf085838187a5b066eccad77b34fc8f1b9dd8||R8a target-specific GPU interfaces; R8b a browser vertical slice (Coaxial is the wasm32 probe).||\n09a3|09a36809f54c8b000eeb983ae16838bdfb11b6a9d6b2621a5a65f46a74351fab||Transitive effect summaries for allocation, host I/O, clocks and randomness; strict math; deterministic jobs.||\ncd0d|cd0d1ea4a618997d6af848f9514bc6e5a3247eaadee5df6df3b76b41a137002d||The remaining semantic work moves into Coax in reviewable slices.||\n3daf|3dafb6d9d2eb1c2bd4d46ad572a9aea0808d0611a2afe3d5034a2bbbb478aede||R11a restricted procedure-body replacement (unchanged-layout Mac experiment first); R11b resident semantics and transactional migration.||\nff44|ff44560d1891c10bf3c7a6a0d0e47fdcbeff0063086ec6528c1b76736f764c3c||The C backend stays the reference; a fast native debug backend only when profiling shows C compilation is the bottleneck.||\n47b1|47b1de82fd67af95ad4ce28f2164dc8812c48fd30ae27cec4b49f99aa824c2e0||socket_open(url), socket_send(id, ptr, len), socket_close(id); open/frame/close/error delivered through the inbox as new message kinds; at most 4 sockets; text frames only.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/web/host.js\\n- apps/openagents-web/ui.coax|A probe page connects to relay.openagents.com, sends a REQ and draws the frame count\\.Closing and errors arrive as inbox messages (#test with a fake inbox)|10-28 15:11 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Probe narrowed: the probe page is /project/coax itself; its header chip drew the frame count (198 frames from relay.openagents.com in headless Chrome). Ids: socket_open(url) returns 0..3 or -1; events are message kinds 256 + 4*id + event (0 opened, 1 frame, 2 closed, 3 error). The C face drains a Coax command queue into the imports, since #foreign takes scalars only.\\.10-28 15:11 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Done in df008f96a4: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/df008f96a4\nd223|d2231dfceab3e2e404cb4c4bcf29a0d11ae02857a5ba4fbb1ee0331384b2e14d||coax/lib/nostr/json.coax: tokens with byte ranges, depth 16, string unescape into caller buffers (all JSON escapes, surrogate pairs), integer parsing to 2^53, refusal of anything over limits; writer appending to a caller buffer.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/nostr/json.coax|JSONTestSuite y_/n_ cases relevant to RFC 8259 (pinned subset) behave correctly\\.No allocation (checked by building with a trapping allocator)\\.Parses every event the relay returns for the coax project (fixture captured from relay.openagents.com)|10-28 15:16 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:JSONTestSuite 1ef36fa pinned: 267 y_/n_ cases in coax/lib/nostr/fixtures/json_suite.coax; 16 left out (not UTF-8, over 4 KiB, or a control byte a Coax literal can't hold), listed in the file; json.coax's own tests cover bad UTF-8 byte by byte and depth 17. No-allocation check: coax/tests/nostr.py CoaxJsonTests links it with a malloc/calloc/realloc/free that abort and parses all 212 captured frames.\\.10-28 15:16 CDT\\:claude-live-1\\:Done in 8f23a77f35: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/8f23a77f35\nc29a|c29a2169fbe2992a82613bd23599354fa629e325e7131fb5f7d79974aabdd0c2|10-28 15:17 CDT|The real project page holds a WebSocket to relay.openagents.com and redraws as events arrive: no snapshots, no release needed to show a claim, a plan, a note, a status or a reorder. The host only moves bytes (host-socket-pipe); Coax parses the relay's JSON, keeps the project's events (REQ with authors = the project key; the relay checks signatures until project-page-verify lands), folds them the way coax/web/project/model.ts does (issues, revisions, statuses, claims, releases, plans, notes, commits, the order record) into the tables project.coax draws, and redraws. Subscriptions stay open after EOSE so new events land live; reconnect with backoff; the header shows LIVE, CONNECTING or OFFLINE instead of a snapshot time. The build-time tables stay only as the first paint until the socket's first EOSE. The demo page keeps its samples.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/project.coax\\n- apps/openagents-web/project/coax/|A claim, a plan update and a done published with publish.ts show on the production page within 2 s, with no release\\.Moving a task (publish.ts move) reorders the live page within 2 s\\.#test: the Coax fold of a captured relay transcript equals model.ts fold() of the same events (same rows, order, plans, log)\\.Killing the socket shows OFFLINE, and it reconnects with backoff\\.No TypeScript beyond the host byte pipe; check-visuals passes|\nb554|b554abc876c574f63cbf357b55bd2ed7feb8303be2892e717877bd239d7505d7||The cast pose, robots/body capsules and player collision run through a repeatable C ABI harness against a pinned native reference (coax0 0.13.0).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 4830ad9c30: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f\nd8c8|d8c8a4d1122f00c9d9c575c6b59dd1befc5d496763deb813d6068fdd6b366059||LLDB breakpoints, stepping, values, stacks, diagnostics and sanitizer traces map to Coax source on Mac and a Simulator app (coax0 0.13.0).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 4830ad9c30: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/4830ad9c30ef749d12c75cb57e35ea7ecff2ff2f\n9527|95273c87481fc686aa436c637bcb90fb658c94570b989e8cc686adcc2da0c03e||The Coax pose kernel passes the unchanged 5% median gate: 1.034x native unoptimized, 0.807x app profile, 0.740x release; reference, harness and budget frozen.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in ff83c9d959: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/ff83c9d959f2d9d94b676b16a441039c30c7f569\n7c2f|7c2f5867576bf90374a3264acbea6039e72d660b8eeb8e8d676d8ca584d9b5c6|10-28 15:03 CDT|CLI version, accepted-feature tables and book status generated from one source, with a publication drift check; implementation, schema and introduction versions kept distinct.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Version, feature tables and book status are generated, not hand-edited\\.A drift check fails when a published copy disagrees with the source|10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Codex thread 01a17379 is on this now (single-source release/status generation and drift checks), with a subagent on another roadmap slice.\n57b3|57b3bc4877bf63ea786de351f3616835ffce903546500fda8bdeefc38457fc5f||Agree a frame-tail budget, then measure the Coax kernels on a named phone: CPU time, tails, copies, allocations and GPU upload, with raw results and dispersion retained.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|A tail budget is written down before optimizing\\.Device runs retained with dispersion; the owner's device step is in NEEDS_OWNER.md|\nd383|d3838817c77b34f32eb9006479c4cebb108e1c73a327b8d602da0ba436e8ded2||Load/parse/check, compile-time work, generation, C compilation, link, assets, launch and GPU preparation; generated C size and peak compiler memory.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|A report attributes every stage for clean and warm builds\\.The largest bottleneck is named with its numbers|\n9d2e|9d2e29f53d1ab109714ebaa9f38cf47c8fcbd14c51218099511930f244ecfa54||Define who reviews changes to invariants, oracles and verification policy, enforced outside the compiler on owned infrastructure, including moves into unmarked helpers.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|The policy is written and enforced by a check outside the compiler\\.A change that weakens a check and its code together is refused without review|\nc296|c296d48f949f9decc5f96333e8d34b113ff066c08a40fbb51af21223c00fdaff||A versioned design and migration for checked arithmetic with explicit wrapping, profile metadata in artifacts and cache keys, and same-profile unoptimized/optimized conformance vectors (overflow, casts, shifts, division edges, evaluation order, cleanup, f32 literal rounding).\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Profiles recorded in artifact metadata\\.Conformance vectors pass in both optimization levels|\nccba|ccba52ff7f1b14e8beb1f74deef63ab443c5dfe4fd80deab1369bc5cb45b8446||An optional native check executable runs pinned inputs through the evaluator and the emitted unoptimized and optimized procedures and compares values, traps and buffer writes.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Seeded evaluator/emitter defects are caught\\.Mismatches minimised and kept as regressions|\n3c97|3c97013cfd742dccd08ffc61f5ef2987590d2bcf3d27a35a3fb228ca00303f57||Every claim bound to source, compiler, target, profile, selection and budgets, with outcomes passed, counterexample, inconclusive, infrastructure error and not checked.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|coax test and coax mutate write the record\\.Missing execution is never a pass|\nf535|f53502bac1b51795d1e3c859655a73d663418b065082d9881662add29ce18c6e||Change a kernel, add a field, repair a type error, update a protocol adapter; pinned revisions, tools and budgets; measure accepted completion, repair iterations and edit-to-result time.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Four tasks pinned with oracles agents can't edit\\.A first run's numbers recorded|\n963b|963ba9fc751a7e575ad782f6635f6bcafca01bd3b5567d4990f3b95e6385cecb||Declaration and content identities, explicit target descriptions, original spans, basic namespaces and minimal inspectable procedure lowering, pinned with differential fixtures and independent oracles.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|Differential fixtures pass against independent oracles|\nca69|ca69f93a896a77f083747dc30d49d5de3420f174748ced153f5ed6aafd9b5ccd||coax fmt and evidence reporting using today's compiler APIs; typed queries and revision-bound fixes follow R1a.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|coax fmt is idempotent over the repository's Coax files|\n07c2|07c2bc1acfda2ce3c5cd3c98b17836e42c3a541171ac557bf4cb2067bf8a6b70||E0383 rejects straightforward local-array view and string returns.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||10-28 15:03 CDT\\:codex-coax\\:Done in 9d0f246ba1: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/9d0f246ba1b95ae0a491cce8e6cb15f4a1de3d21\n6541|6541812581360075e6a12e196f4773d4ab5c4a90b39a409098eb60f916833c80||Typed results and optionals, exhaustive switch, propagation and exhaustive cleanup, with one real asynchronous adapter.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.|The spec's R2a examples compile and their checks pass|\n76ba|76bad4951d0c2dc57eda7e4522070c27e951ab21a06177f05f1c5f0368b273b7||Generic copyable values and non-owning operations over fixed storage.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n791f|791f07997d9b98b2a86b2f3157fcd71db650fca9cfa838f634998d3bbc9d92ee||Narrow derivation (equality, formatting, serialization) over concrete, already-checked types.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n0c13|0c13c6ed2696572356537f5a6b8340b3431a779cae2f96ae1bbb5df6f6f3f414||The unchanged-layout Mac replacement experiment: swap a procedure body in a running app.\\n\\nRoadmap: coax/ROADMAP.md.||\n72f7|72f75267f47e6638ec4eb026ddaf506a8efc543f08c80f53997b5813d29399bd||Every Nostr integration on openagents.com runs in Coax: SHA-256, secp256k1, BIP-340, ECDH, NIP-44, NIP-59, events, bech32, relay client. Specification: coax/nostr.md.\\n\\nSpecification: coax/nostr.md in the openagents repository.||10-28 14:38 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:process: claims, notes and done are now NIP-22 comments the page draws (fdd3a57565); workers run release.sh after each claim and done\n3514|351453fe6079dc23cec9f2ee0c28604295624d7a68a042753a1d52718ac24ac7||Byte helpers, SHA-256, HMAC, HKDF, PBKDF2, ChaCha20, hex and base64 in Coax, each against its official vectors.||\n2a73|2a737385f645eff09bfab959a061fb5f9df78d4cc003826519c97795b58f7a48||secp256k1 field elements (10x26) and scalars mod n, with inversion and square root, proven bounds and differential tests.||\n415a|415aa469756162d066415e784a66144b7217e3c58a11390b85bf34eeec6f3c82||Points, wNAF dual multiplication and BIP-340 verification.||\n3021|3021a5a2952db48a66482951d1f2cc86b59131ad7911ab95ae34e1992c833e92||Fixed-base comb, constant-time ladder, BIP-340 signing and x-only ECDH, with timing evidence.||\nca06|ca06a75181b2db380cb5e9a2522c0910d784670c1c2ce0f5f245e9be5e3793b9||Version 2 encryption, seals and gift wraps that interoperate with spec implementations.||\nabf5|abf5ecb9864de2dd92cf46a47832768354bf2a3a49178ab240fdfb6d49a14844||Bounded JSON, NIP-01 events, filters, bech32 and NIP-19, JCS and the 3188 artifact envelope.||\n4d8f|4d8f39528a7967fc4cd9697e8d3bef293df9111b75f09bb4318587e0c83bbe71||Host random, socket and storage imports; the relay state machine with NIP-42 AUTH.||\n6c0d|6c0d25259ca6ef6ff8b2ff046edc5a0b95713d6a9dfabfabe916a0ab8aca35ea||The hidden deck opens with no TypeScript: opener, gate, sealer and injector in Coax; the INVARIANTS change.||\n5653|56535bb0d3eb500391d723bb4693a660cdcbe8c97c07a5f7a91a2b2900987376||/project/coax reads its project, tasks and order from the relay and signs claims in the page.||\n7807|78074c5465846ad23865195fc9436c66143220a3164d8cefa6e0062de3c9b373||Small compiler features and fixes the stack wants; none blocks M0-M2.||\n9680|968040980c4cc123132f11495fc8b6279fadc183015b1b17bf2026b1e02f89e9||The deliverable: open openagents.com/signin, scan its QR code with the OpenAgents mobile app, approve, and the website is signed in as your Nostr key. The key never leaves the phone. NIP-46 (Nostr Connect) between page and phone over relay.openagents.com, NIP-98 HTTP auth to the server, no WorkOS. The same Coax Nostr library runs on the phone (compiled to C), in the page (wasm) and on the server (native).||\na7e7|a7e7967191ef28d9affbd6aca2c6f4c328e5a8a6e71f4eafcf7e75da4a5e700f||t[0].count[b] += 1 on an array field reached through a view generates C that does not compile (found building the project page). Fix the emitter and add a regression test.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/src/emit_c.cpp\\n- coax/tests/|A test with t[0].count[b] += 1 (and -=, *=, \\p=) through a view compiles and runs under ASan\\.coax/tests pass|10-28 14:51 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:Done in e2f8432ea2: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/e2f8432ea2\\.10-28 14:51 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:The plain b-index case already compiled; the bug was a call in an index (t[0].count[f(i)] += 1, and plain = too): the emitter took the address of a comma expression. Checks: tests/pass/compound_view (debug+release), tests/native.py under ASan/UBSan, coax/tests/run.sh all green.\nb17d|b17db3e238f978ff3415d8c228eb42683128322d8ba8212a81b823eabc4748a7||Add value_barrier(x: u64) -> u64 (and u32) that the optimizer cannot see through: native emits __asm__(\"\" : \"+r\"(x)), wasm32 emits a call to a non-inlined identity. Document it in coax/spec.md 9.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/src/\\n- coax/spec.md\\n- coax/tests/|Generated C for a masked select compiled with clang -O2 contains no conditional branch on the masked value (checked by objdump in a test script)\\.coax/tests pass|10-28 15:01 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:Surprise: the checker seed refresh runs coax mutate on checker.coax (~6 min); 13 mutants in the new branch survived, so the new code needs its own #forall before the seed can refresh.\\.10-28 15:21 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:Done in b9a5f216f0: https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/commit/b9a5f216f0\\.10-28 15:21 CDT\\:claude-queue-1\\:Checks: tests/constant_time.py (objdump: ct_select and ct_select32 have no conditional branch at clang -O2 on arm64; wasm32 calls the identity), checker #test/#forall 554 and mutate 3777/3777 killed, coax/tests/run.sh 88 passed. One failure is not from this change: tests/fail/ct_view expects E0409 but gets E0383 since 9d0f246ba1 (returned borrows of local arrays).\n0ad5|0ad56dd04b3014052d86aa154588c49234d1ff82c0d221eeaf254802e9b14202||Add add_wrap, sub_wrap, mul_wrap, rotl, rotr for u32/u64 that never trap in any build mode. SHA-256 and ChaCha20 can use them instead of computing in u64 and masking.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/src/\\n- coax/spec.md|Tests for each op at the type's limits in debug and --release\\.coax/tests pass|\ncead|cead935db7ace271e21900abbc2d2df3a2de667b26fde55a957a22b9e6cd446c||Add mul_wide(a, b: u64) -> (hi, lo: u64): C emits unsigned __int128; wasm32 emits a four-multiply split. Enables a 5x52 field on native later.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/src/\\n- coax/spec.md|Random and edge vectors match a reference computed with __int128 on native and in wasm32 (node or a headless page)\\.coax/tests pass|\n7e39|7e3934a9c0d037a0aedd82652a39ce54157d1a653cd8100c4e7bdf66a00c70ca||A way to declare fields and statements that exist only in development builds (spec 10.5 conditional compilation, the minimal slice), so field elements can carry magnitudes in debug and not in release.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/src/\\n- coax/spec.md|A struct with a debug-only field has a smaller size_of in --release; statements under the debug condition are absent from release C\\.coax/tests pass|\n993f|993ff555b07d19c09c6be7bb909c88dca8843b422aba400720be87c0c34add90||coax/lib/crypto/bytes.coax: load/store be32/le32/be64/le64, ct_eq over views (returns a mask), ct_select for u32/u64 and views, zeroize through the value barrier (a #foreign no-op until the intrinsic lands).\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/bytes.coax|#test covers every helper at boundaries\\.coax mutate coax/lib/crypto/bytes.coax: no surviving mutants|\nef11|ef110244163f42af67495669bf9b2dad025e3f1fe652c59637927a9640315259||Create coax/tests/vectors/ with the files listed in coax/nostr.md 9.1 (NIST SHA-256 subset, RFC 4231, 5869, 7914, 8439, BIP-340 CSV, Wycheproof ecdh_secp256k1, NIP-44 vectors, BIP-173) and SOURCES.md recording URL, retrieval date and SHA-256 of each.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/tests/vectors/\\n- coax/tests/vectors/SOURCES.md|Every file in SOURCES.md matches its recorded SHA-256 (a check script)\\.No file is modified from upstream|\n0e80|0e80305628f5865f8215377b9ea71ee3a220fce2813307c148f3319fc0508643||tools/coax-nostr/vectors.sh builds each module with coax c -> clang with ASan/UBSan and runs a C driver per vector file, reporting pass/fail per row. Heavy vectors run here; small ones also run as #test.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- tools/coax-nostr/vectors.sh\\n- tools/coax-nostr/vectors/|Runs on macOS with the existing toolchain\\.Fails loudly on a single wrong row (tested by corrupting one expected value in a temp copy)|\n6784|67846980e155bd984c7c9b0791191732f3a7921615bc413bbf7ecd168ca1b292||coax/lib/crypto/sha256.coax: init/update/final over views, one-shot sha256, and tagged_hash(tag, msg) = SHA256(SHA256(tag)\\p\\pSHA256(tag)\\p\\pmsg) with the three BIP-340 tags' prefixes precomputed with #run.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/sha256.coax|NIST subset and the 1 MiB split-at-every-chunk test pass in the vector runner\\.#test: empty, \"abc\", tagged hash of BIP0340/challenge known value\\.coax mutate: no surviving mutants\\.>= 150 MB/s in wasm32, >= 300 MB/s native (bench printed)|\nf20e|f20e2fcf01473864c4e6a74bda37893d2c7b3705e68e00b759902cb0395b28f9||coax/lib/crypto/hmac.coax and hkdf.coax: hmac_sha256(key, msg), HKDF extract and expand (NIP-44 uses expand with 76 bytes).\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/hmac.coax\\n- coax/lib/crypto/hkdf.coax|RFC 4231 cases 1-7 and RFC 5869 cases 1-3 pass\\.coax mutate: no surviving mutants|\n4747|4747fbcbf213e5c9af2f8f7d793a9b19f3b0d9ef23259ea776670da780296456||coax/lib/crypto/pbkdf2.coax for the phrase gate (210,000 rounds); reuse the HMAC inner/outer state per round.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/pbkdf2.coax|RFC 7914 11 vectors pass\\.210,000 rounds take under 400 ms in wasm32 in Chrome|\n5fc9|5fc9d914022e871930f5eaacbb29f1615373f22063c0dc14c89c0f0e09f2cde8||coax/lib/crypto/chacha20.coax per RFC 8439 2.3-2.4: 32-byte key, 12-byte nonce, 32-bit counter; xor stream into caller buffer.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- coax/lib/crypto/chacha20.coax|RFC 8439 2.3.2, 2.4.2, A.1 and A.2 pass\\.coax mutate: no 