3bc1ce6da378ed209075fd3faf24d4e5384f28a1a3b8||Byte mode, error correction M, versions 1 to 15, mask selection by the standard penalty rules; output a module grid the page draws as HUD strokes or quads.|Matches a reference encoder's module grids for 20 fixed strings including a 300-byte nostrconnect URI\\.A phone camera (the iOS scanner test) decodes a rendered code|\na1d8|a1d85392c1cdcda73b83d8c22b82c959267620ea119aac3408b4e077dc0b13d1||The app's QR scanner recognises nostrconnect:// codes, shows the site and what it asks for in an approval sheet, and on approval runs the NIP-46 signer for that session; the session shows in Settings and can be ended there.|Simulator UI test: a fixture QR image opens the approval sheet; approve connects to a local relay\\.Ending the session in Settings makes later requests fail|\n0af1|0af19f0b640e3bfc544a89722f0f5af6d9601dd5d2ebadbd28fccc54f8d7eac9||A native Coax server route POST /auth/nostr takes a NIP-98 kind 27235 event (url, method, payload hash, created_at within 60 s, unused id), verifies it with the Coax verifier, and sets an HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict session cookie bound to the pubkey. Admin pubkeys come from config. No WorkOS.|Tests: valid event accepted; wrong url, method, stale time, replayed id and bad signature refused\\.The cookie carries no key material and expires|\nc8dd|c8ddf047e6f45e3cb209922826bd0a56284dbb200afff3c52b33cf566b927490||A Coaxial page draws the QR (HUD, Filament), waits for the phone, then asks it to sign the NIP-98 event and posts it to /auth/nostr. Shows who is signed in (npub, short) and sign out. Plain text in the hidden main for agents.|check-visuals passes; real-Chrome screenshots of waiting and signed-in states\\.The page never holds the user's secret key|\n73ce|73ce5c1cdf68fecacb68149159896ca1d245fe253597cde984cc61a0310aa7c4||The deliverable test: the iOS simulator scans the QR shown by the page (fixture image of the live page's code), approves, and the page reaches the signed-in state with the server session bound to the phone's pubkey. Device run is an owner step in NEEDS_OWNER.md.|Simulator plus headless page run passes against a local relay and server\\.Staging run passes against relay.openagents.com\\.Device step recorded for the owner|\nc969|c96951910dfb701627c5e9888c5265343c262f128b2471853a440fd3dc487aee||Once Schnorr verification lands, the live page checks every event's id and signature in Coax before folding it (<= 4 ms of verification per frame, the rest queued), and stops relying on the relay's check.\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n- apps/openagents-web/project.coax|Unverified events never appear; a count of rows still checking is shown\\.A forged event injected through a test relay is refused and counted|\n";
